@page "/privacy"
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
    ViewData["Wide"] = true;
    Layout = "_CenteredLayout";

    var operatorName = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Settings.OperatorName) ? "the operator of this server" : Model.Settings.OperatorName;
    var contact = Model.Settings.PrivacyContact;

    string Hours(TimeSpan time) => time.TotalHours == 1 ? "1 hour" : $"{time.TotalHours:0.#} hours";
    string Days(TimeSpan time) => $"{time.TotalDays:0} days";
}

<h1 class="h3 mb-3">Privacy policy</h1>

<div class="alert alert-secondary">
    <strong>@Model.Settings.ServerName is a third-party service.</strong>
    It is not provided, operated or endorsed by VATSIM.
</div>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">About this service</h2>
<p>
    This server relays CPDLC and ADS-C messages between air traffic controllers on VATSIM and aircraft on the
    ACARS network. <strong>@operatorName</strong> operates this server. In this policy, "the operator" is
    @operatorName.
</p>
@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(contact))
{
    <p>
        For questions about your data, or to ask the operator to delete your data, use this contact:
        <a href="@PrivacyContactFormat.ToHref(contact)">@contact</a>.
    </p>
}
<p>
    The server uses the open source <a href="https://github.com/YuKitsune/CPDLCPlugin">CPDLC Plugin</a> software.
    The authors of the software do not operate this server, and they cannot see its data.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">The data that the server collects</h2>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Your VATSIM account.</strong> You log in with VATSIM Connect. VATSIM gives the server your CID and
        your full name. The server also asks VATSIM for your VATSIM details (for example, your rating and division),
        but it does not use or keep them. The server does not get your email address or your password.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Controllers.</strong> When you connect with the vatSys plugin, the server records your CID, your name,
        your callsign and your station while you are connected.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Administrators.</strong> The server records the CID and the name of each administrator, and the date
        when they became an administrator.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Flight data.</strong> The server receives aircraft callsigns, CPDLC messages and ADS-C reports
        (position, level and time) from the ACARS network.
        @if (Model.Settings.VatsimStatusEnabled)
        {
            <text>It also reads aircraft positions from the public VATSIM status data.</text>
        }
        CPDLC messages can contain free text from pilots and controllers.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Logs.</strong> The server log records events, for example logins, plugin connections and messages.
        A log entry can contain your CID, your name, your callsign and the text of a message.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Cookies.</strong> The server uses only the cookies that are necessary for it to operate: one cookie
        that keeps you logged in, and short-term cookies that protect the login and the forms. The server does not use
        cookies for analytics or advertising.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>IP addresses.</strong> The server does not record your IP address. The hosting provider of the server
        can record it (see <a href="#third-parties">Third parties</a>).
    </li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">How the server uses the data</h2>
<p>The server uses the data only to operate the service:</p>
<ul>
    <li>to identify you, and to give administrators access to the configuration,</li>
    <li>to relay CPDLC and ADS-C messages between controllers and aircraft,</li>
    <li>to show the connected controllers and aircraft, and the messages,</li>
    <li>to find and correct problems.</li>
</ul>
<p>The operator does not sell the data, and does not use it for advertising or analytics.</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who can see the data</h2>
<ul>
    <li>
        Each VATSIM user who logs in to this server can see the CPDLC and ADS-C pages. These pages show the name and
        the CID of each connected controller, the callsigns of the aircraft, the CPDLC messages and the ADS-C data.
    </li>
    <li>Controllers who use the plugin see the CPDLC messages and the ADS-C data of the aircraft.</li>
    <li>Administrators can also see the server log and the raw messages to and from the ACARS network.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4" id="third-parties">Third parties</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>VATSIM</strong> operates VATSIM Connect, which identifies you when you log in.</li>
    <li>
        <strong>The ACARS network</strong> (for example, <a href="https://www.hoppie.nl/acars/">Hoppie's ACARS</a>)
        carries the CPDLC and ADS-C messages to and from the aircraft. It receives the station, the callsigns and
        the messages. It does not receive your CID or your name.
    </li>
    <li><strong>The hosting provider</strong> of the server stores the database and can record network data, for example IP addresses.</li>
    <li>
        <strong>jsDelivr</strong> (cdn.jsdelivr.net) supplies the styles and scripts of the web pages. Your browser
        downloads them from jsDelivr, so jsDelivr receives your IP address.
    </li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">How long the server keeps the data</h2>
<div class="table-responsive">
    <table class="table table-sm">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Data</th>
                <th>Kept</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>Login cookie</td>
                <td>Until you log out, or after @Hours(Model.SessionLifetime) without activity. A restart of the server also logs out all users.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Plugin authentication (CID, name and token)</td>
                <td>The token is valid for @Days(Model.PluginTokenLifetime). When you select Log out in the plugin, the server deletes it. The record of an expired token stays in the database.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Administrators</td>
                <td>Until an administrator removes them.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Connected controllers</td>
                <td>Only in memory, until the controller disconnects.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Aircraft connections</td>
                <td>Until the connection ends, or after @Model.Settings.AircraftConnectionTimeoutMinutes minutes without contact from the aircraft.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>CPDLC messages</td>
                <td>@Model.Settings.DialogueRetentionHours hours from the start of the dialogue.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>ADS-C contracts and reports</td>
                <td>Until the contract ends, or after @Model.Settings.AdscContractTimeoutMinutes minutes without ADS-C activity. The server keeps only the latest report of each contract.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>ADS-C message log</td>
                <td>Only in memory, for @Hours(Model.AdscMessageLogRetention), and not more than the last @Model.AdscMessageLogCapacity messages.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Server log</td>
                <td>Only in memory, the last @Model.LogCapacity entries. A restart deletes them. The hosting provider can keep a copy of the log output for a period that the operator sets.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Raw ACARS messages</td>
                <td>Only in memory, the last @Model.TrafficLogCapacity requests of each ACARS connection. A restart deletes them.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>
    The vatSys plugin keeps your token on your computer, encrypted for your Windows account. The plugin log on your
    computer is kept for 5 days by default.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Security</h2>
<p>
    The server keeps only a hash of each plugin token. It encrypts the ACARS network codes with a key that is not in
    the database. Use the server only over HTTPS.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your choices</h2>
<ul>
    <li>To remove the plugin authentication, select Log out in the SETUP window of the plugin.</li>
    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(contact))
    {
        <li>To ask for a copy of your data, or to ask the operator to delete it, use the contact: <a href="@PrivacyContactFormat.ToHref(contact)">@contact</a>.</li>
    }
    else
    {
        <li>To ask for a copy of your data, or to ask the operator to delete it, speak to an administrator of this server.</li>
    }
    <li>If you do not accept this policy, do not log in to this server and do not connect the plugin to it.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Changes to this policy</h2>
<p class="mb-0">The operator can change this policy. This page always shows the current policy.</p>
